  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Using two relations: JOIN"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A JOIN combines tuples of two relations that satisfy a condition, usually equality of a common attribute (an equi-join). It can be written as a Cartesian product with a WHERE condition, or with JOIN ... ON. Table aliases (STUDENT S) keep the query short; columns with the same name are written as S.RollNo and F.RollNo."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Equi-join: WHERE S.RollNo = F.RollNo"
    },
    {
     "en": "Or: STUDENT S JOIN FEES F ON S.RollNo = F.RollNo"
    },
    {
     "en": "Without a join condition you get the full Cartesian product"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A join matches rows of two tables on a common column, such as roll number. Without the join condition, you get every possible pair of rows.",
    "kn": "ಜೋಡಣೆ ಎರಡು ಕೋಷ್ಟಕಗಳ ಸಾಲುಗಳನ್ನು ಕ್ರಮಸಂಖ್ಯೆಯಂತಹ ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯ ಕಾಲಂ ಮೇಲೆ ಹೊಂದಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಷರತ್ತು ಇಲ್ಲದಿದ್ದರೆ ಎಲ್ಲ ಸಾಧ್ಯ ಜೋಡಿಗಳು ಬರುತ್ತವೆ."
   }
  },
